          <li><strong>Voltage Drop Engineering:</strong> Every long-distance circuit is designed with properly sized conductors to deliver full voltage at the charger location.</li>
          <li><strong>Detached Structure Experience:</strong> We install subpanels, underground feeders, and independent grounding systems for detached garages, barns, and shops.</li>
          <li><strong>Multi-Jurisdiction Familiarity:</strong> We file permits through both City of Issaquah and WA L&I, depending on whether the property falls within city limits or unincorporated King County.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct Communication:</strong> We explain what your property needs, what the options are, and what each option involves, then let you decide the best path forward.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Our Service Process for Preston Properties</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Detailed Phone Consultation:</strong> We gather property details including home vintage, panel type, building layout, distance from panel to parking area, well pump specifications, and vehicle model.</li>
          <li><strong>On-Site Property Survey:</strong> Our electrician inspects the panel, measures distances, evaluates terrain for conduit routing, and calculates load capacity and voltage drop.</li>
          <li><strong>Engineered repair:</strong> We build the circuit to the specific engineering requirements of your property—proper wire gauge, properly sized subpanels, surge protection, and NEC-compliant grounding.</li>
          <li><strong>Full-Load Verification:</strong> We charge your vehicle under full load, measuring voltage at the charger to confirm the repair delivers designed performance.</li>
        </ol>

        <p>
          Call <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a> to discuss your Preston EV charger project. Whether your property has a modern garage attached to the house or a detached barn 100 feet from the panel, we engineer repairs that charge reliably for years to come.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

